<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolesław III Wrymouth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1086–1138</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolesław III Wrymouth was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> from 1102 to 1138. He conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>, defended Poland against the German emperor Henry V in 1109 and promoted the Christianisation of the Pomeranians. His testament of 1138 divided the realm among his sons, with the senior duke ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a>, beginning almost two centuries of fragmentation into duchies such as Greater Poland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iii-wrymouth.jpg" alt="Bolesław III Wrymouth" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Societas Scientiarum Plocensis (Towarzystwo Naukowe Płockie), based on the sketches of Jerzy Mazuś. · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boleslaw_III_Wrymouth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
